rformance problems like N+1 queries, unnecessary JSON marshaling, and string concatenation in loops, with concrete fixes that reduced response times from 2 seconds to 50ms.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7ffb2836886233640cc42b6d645e1b47?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-01T07:02:59.774Z"},{"id":"gn3YJmYWj","title":"Go libs I don't use but are popular","url":"https://developer20.com/go-libs-i-dont-use/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/go-libs-i-don-t-use-but-are-popular-gn3yjmywj","summary":"The post discusses popular Go libraries that the author chooses to avoid, highlighting their drawbacks, especially in larger projects. It covers sqlmock, GORM, and gorilla mux, providing reasons like brittleness in tests, complexity in schema migrations, and performance bottlenecks. Alternative approaches such as integration testing, using sqlx, and sticking to Go\u2019s standard net/http package are suggested for more maintainable and scalable solutions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"FAv3nKlzT","title":"Testing code with unpredictable or random output","url":"https://developer20.com/test-with-random/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/testing-code-with-unpredictable-or-random-output-fav3nklzt","summary":"Learn how to test functions in Go that involve randomness. Techniques discussed include using dependency injection, seeding random values, and statistical testing to handle unpredictable outputs while ensuring code quality and test reliability.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-08-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2W8PXkS12","title":"\u00b7 Developer 2.0","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Heap-Escape-Analysis-in-Go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/developer-2-0-2w8pxks12","summary":"The Go compiler relocates variables to the heap instead of the stack if it cannot guarantee the variable won't outlive the caller function. By using the `-gcflags=\"-m\"` parameter, developers can perform heap escape analysis, receiving output that shows compile optimizations. Numerous factors, such as using interfaces, can lead to variables escaping to the heap.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-25T07:57:25.843Z"},{"id":"YkHyhJbRA","title":"How to hash and compare passwords in Go","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Passwords-in-Go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-hash-and-compare-passwords-in-go-ykhyhjbra","summary":"Learn how to hash and compare passwords in Go using bcrypt.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"iRxbOcgVK","title":"Flattening the Package Structure","url":"https://developer20.com/flattening-package-structure/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/flattening-the-package-structure-irxbocgvk","summary":"This post explores the journey of structuring the 'productcatalog' package, highlighting the impact of overengineering, the importance of simplicity in coding, and the benefits of outside-in testing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gmKlitLbO","title":"Password policies","url":"https://developer20.com/password-policies/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/password-policies-gmklitlbo","summary":"This post discusses the implementation of password policies in Go, including creating an interface for policies, making them configurable using functional-style code, and handling errors. It also mentions plans to add a policy to restrict leaked passwords and the use of the haveibeenpwned API.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"SpahettDB","title":"My Smart Home high-level architecture","url":"https://developer20.com/smart-home-architecture/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/my-smart-home-high-level-architecture-spahettdb","summary":"A homeowner shares their high-level architecture for creating a smart home, focusing on the core requirements, the choice of Loxone as the base system, and the use of Raspberry Pi as a hub for third-party devices.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gAhMHs3Lm","title":"Honestly about why Go sucks (or not)","url":"https://developer20.com/hate-go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/honestly-about-why-go-sucks-or-not--gahmhs3lm","summary":"Go has its pros and cons, including arguments against its lack of function overloading and default values for arguments, the recent introduction of generics in version 1.18, and previous challenges with dependency management in the Go ecosystem.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-07-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"UMyvbvCaR","title":"gRPC with SSL/TLS","url":"https://developer20.com/grpc-ssl/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/grpc-with-ssl-tls-umyvbvcar","summary":"gRPC supports authentication with SSL/TLS. Configuring it with just a few lines of code. The certificate can be generated using openssl or certstrap.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-11-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"gn3YJmYWj","title":"Go libs I don't use but are popular","url":"https://developer20.com/go-libs-i-dont-use/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/go-libs-i-don-t-use-but-are-popular-gn3yjmywj","summary":"The post discusses popular Go libraries that the author chooses to avoid, highlighting their drawbacks, especially in larger projects. It covers sqlmock, GORM, and gorilla mux, providing reasons like brittleness in tests, complexity in schema migrations, and performance bottlenecks. Alternative approaches such as integration testing, using sqlx, and sticking to Go\u2019s standard net/http package are suggested for more maintainable and scalable solutions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"2W8PXkS12","title":"\u00b7 Developer 2.0","url":"https://developer20.com/notes/Heap-Escape-Analysis-in-Go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/developer-2-0-2w8pxks12","summary":"The Go compiler relocates variables to the heap instead of the stack if it cannot guarantee the variable won't outlive the caller function. By using the `-gcflags=\"-m\"` parameter, developers can perform heap escape analysis, receiving output that shows compile optimizations. Numerous factors, such as using interfaces, can lead to variables escaping to the heap.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-25T07:57:25.843Z"},{"id":"qFuGh5ogx","title":"How to send multiple variables via channel in golang?","url":"https://developer20.com/how-to-send-multiple-variables-via-channel-in-golang/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-send-multiple-variables-via-channel-in-golang--qfugh5ogx","summary":"Learn how to send multiple variables via channels in golang using structs and functions as information carriers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2018-12-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"rxaqboHbh","title":"Golang Tips & Tricks #5 - blank identifier in structs","url":"https://developer20.com/golang-tips-and-trics-v/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/golang-tips-tricks-5---blank-identifier-in-structs-rxaqbohbh","summary":"Learn how to initialize a structure without providing field keys in Go and how to force explicit field key provision. Find out the error that occurs when using a blank identifier in a structure literal.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2019-07-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"V4xIitt5P","title":"History of WWW","url":"https://developer20.com/history-of-www/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/history-of-www-v4xiitt5p","summary":"The history of the WWW began with the theoretical machine called Memex and the creation of languages like GML and SGML. Tim Berners-Lee and Dom Connolly then developed HTML, HTTP, and the first WWW browser, leading to the growth of easily accessible web content.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/179dc324eb65abefe5dac094b9955997?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2018-05-02T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["jooq","metaredux","rbywkly","modernescpp","rustanalyzer"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","ryolu_","kloss_xyz","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"jooq","handle":"jooq","name":"JOOQ","is_squad":false,"x":-6.4117,"y":-3.0802,"cluster_id":1,"posts_colle